{
  "title": "Developer Productivity",
  "uid": "claude-code-dev-productivity",
  "schemaVersion": 27,
  "version": 8,
  "tags": [
    "claude-code",
    "productivity",
    "developer"
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "user",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(claude_code_cost_usage_USD_total, user_email)"
        },
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "selected": true,
          "text": "All",
          "value": [
            "$__all"
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Headline — Leverage, Speed & Efficiency",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1001,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Leverage — agent time vs. your time",
      "description": "Total agent (CLI) active-time ÷ your active-time over the visible range. >1× means the agent did more wall-clock work than you put in by hand. 1× = break-even.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(claude_code_active_time_seconds_total{type=\"cli\",user_email=~\"$user\"}[$__range])) / sum(increase(claude_code_active_time_seconds_total{type=\"user\",user_email=~\"$user\"}[$__range]))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "suffix:×",
          "decimals": 2,
          "displayName": "Leverage",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calc": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Accepted edits per active hour",
      "description": "Accepted code edits (Edit/Write, decision=accept) per hour of ACTIVE engagement, range-wide ratio-of-sums: sum(accepted edits over range) / (sum(active seconds, CLI+user)/3600). A SPEED/cadence signal, NOT quality — read alongside 'First-pass acceptance (%)' (panel 6): rising cadence WITH stable acceptance is healthy; rising cadence WITH falling acceptance is rubber-stamping. Neutral color on purpose: faster isn't automatically better. Judge the trend against your own baseline — no fixed 'good' target. Sparkline shows the trailing shape. user_email filter is cosmetic on this single-user host.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(claude_code_code_edit_tool_decision_total{decision=\"accept\",user_email=~\"$user\"}[$__range])) / (sum(increase(claude_code_active_time_seconds_total{user_email=~\"$user\"}[$__range])) / 3600)",
          "legendFormat": "Edits / active hr"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 1,
          "displayName": "Edits / active hr",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calc": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Cache hit ratio — context served from cache",
      "description": "Share of prompt-context tokens served from the prompt cache: cacheRead / (input + cacheRead + cacheCreation), ratio-of-sums over the visible range. Excludes output tokens. Higher is better — more reused context means lower token cost and faster turns. Healthy multi-turn sessions run ~85-95%; a sustained drop below your own baseline (under ~0.9 yellow, under ~0.7 red) signals cache-unfriendly prompting (volatile/early-changing context, churning CLAUDE.md, or reordered MCP/context load).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(claude_code_token_usage_tokens_total{type=\"cacheRead\",user_email=~\"$user\"}[$__range])) / sum(increase(claude_code_token_usage_tokens_total{type=~\"input|cacheRead|cacheCreation\",user_email=~\"$user\"}[$__range]))"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 1,
          "displayName": "Cache hit",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.7
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.9
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calc": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Friction — where time & attention leak",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "id": 1002,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Tool failure rate by tool (%)",
      "description": "Share of each tool's calls that FAILED (success=false), per tool_name, as a 6h trailing ratio-of-sums (failed/total). Self-normalizing — internalizes call volume, so failing 3% of 4,000 Bash calls is distinguished from failing 50% of 4 calls. This is the dashboard's primary friction signal (Loki, all-user). Watch the RATE, not raw counts: a tool climbing above its own baseline = flaky command, wrong path pattern, or misconfig. A failed call isn't always wasted (a grep that misses still informs the next step). 6h window smooths low-volume tools; gaps are honest (no calls). Legend max = worst spike. Only tools that failed at least once appear.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "100 * (sum by (tool_name)(count_over_time({service_name=\"claude-code\"} | event_name=\"tool_result\" | success=\"false\" [6h])) / sum by (tool_name)(count_over_time({service_name=\"claude-code\"} | event_name=\"tool_result\" [6h])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{tool_name}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "decimals": 1,
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Interruptions — rejected tool calls (by tool)",
      "description": "Tool calls you DECLINED (Loki tool_decision, decision=reject), counted in disjoint per-bucket windows and stacked by tool_name so you see WHICH tool's actions you interrupt most. Read as ATTENTION COST + a steering signal, NOT a quality grade — a reject often means the guardrail worked (you caught drift before it landed). Over 7d, Bash dominates rejects (you decline proposed commands); if that climbs, tighten what the agent may run (allowlist, narrower prompts, CLAUDE.md guidance). Loki is all-user; $user does not narrow it. Disjoint $__interval buckets (no sliding double-count); legend sum = total rejects per tool over the range. Low-frequency (~9/day) so buckets are sparse by nature — read the composition, not bar height.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (tool_name)(count_over_time({service_name=\"claude-code\"} | event_name=\"tool_decision\" | decision=\"reject\" [$__interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{tool_name}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "bars",
            "fillOpacity": 70,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "sum",
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10
      }
    }
  ]
}
